# EXPECT: also binds outside this loop
# ouroboros#187, the read-only twin of interrogated_local_binder: a `for`
# binder over a function local, interrogated, body only reads. The VM
# loop-scopes the binder (7 8 1 7 here, where `local r` ran first), but the
# post-loop read is the other binding's value ONLY if that binding executed
# before the loop -- a `local r is 3` AFTER the loop, or in a not-taken
# branch, makes the VM die 'undefined variable' where the emitted C local
# would read 0 (round-116 critic, pre-existing at HEAD: 7 8 7 0 3 at rc 0).
# The bound-set cannot tell the two apart, so both refuse until a boundness
# bit exists (the #157/#163/#185 class).
define f(q) as:
    local r is q
    for r in [7, 8]:
        print of r
    print of r
    print of (prev of r)
    return 0
f of 1
